{"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivortuning\/tuningsystem\/youngii"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning","doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/TuningSystem"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"youngII"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:10IvorTuning15WellTemperamentV","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"WellTemperament"},{"text":" { ","kind":"text"},{"text":"get","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" }","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Six consecutive fifths from C to F♯ — C→G, G→D, D→A, A→E, E→B, B→F♯ — are each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"narrowed by ⅙ of the Pythagorean comma, equal to 2^(13\/6)\/3 ≈ 698.045 cents.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The remaining six fifths are pure (3:2). The circle closes exactly.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The tempered fifth size is identical to Vallotti, but the tempered segment runs","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from C through F♯ (six sharps) rather than from F through B (six naturals\/flats).","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Published in ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Philosophical Transactions of the Royal Society"}]},{"text":" 90 (1800).","type":"text"}]}]}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/TuningSystem\/youngII"},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"IvorTuning"}],"role":"symbol","title":"youngII","conformance":{"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Self"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"WellTemperament"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"text":"Available when","type":"text"}],"conformancePrefix":[{"text":"Conforms when","type":"text"}]},"symbolKind":"property","fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"youngII"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:10IvorTuning15WellTemperamentV","text":"WellTemperament"}],"extendedModule":"IvorTuning","roleHeading":"Type Property","externalID":"s:10IvorTuning0B6SystemPA2A15WellTemperamentVRszrlE7youngIIAEvpZ"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Young II (Thomas Young, 1800)."}],"references":{"doc://IvorTuning/documentation/IvorTuning/TuningSystem":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivortuning\/tuningsystem","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"TuningSystem","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/TuningSystem","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"TuningSystem","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A type that describes a musical tuning system."}],"title":"TuningSystem"},"doc://IvorTuning/documentation/IvorTuning":{"abstract":[{"text":"Musical pitch, interval, and tuning system types.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning","url":"\/documentation\/ivortuning","title":"IvorTuning","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","type":"topic"},"doc://IvorTuning/documentation/IvorTuning/WellTemperament":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivortuning\/welltemperament","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"